  "summary": "Import-time exfiltration of working-directory listing to remote tunnel",
  "details": "On `import MRCL2`, the top-level __init__.py loads.core, which as a module-level side effect opens a raw TCP socket to the hardcoded host glicv-13-205-45-209.run.pinggy-free.link on port 35617 (a Pinggy free-tunnel relay) and sends the output of os.listdir('.') to it. The package is advertised as a document integrity utility; the directory-listing exfiltration is undocumented, unconditional, and fires on import without any caller action. The destination is an anonymous ephemeral tunnel not associated with the package's declared purpose.",
